{
    "background_story": "Cairo was a majestic Arabian stallion with a shiny black coat and a spirited personality. He was a prized possession of the wealthy Sheikh's stable, known for his impressive jumping skills and endurance. However, Cairo's life took a dramatic turn when he contracted tetanus, a bacterial infection that caused him to develop a severe case of opisthotonos. His body would arch backward, his legs stiffening in a rigid pose, as he struggled to move. Despite the challenges, Cairo's loyal groom, Ali, nursed him back to health with patience and care. With time, Cairo recovered, but the experience left him with a newfound appreciation for life. He became a therapy horse, helping people with disabilities and injuries, and Ali remained by his side, a testament to the unbreakable bond between them.",
